.Dd March 2026
.Dt BFCODEC 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm bfcodec
.Nd encode or decode files using BFCodec (Blowfish-derived) cipher with CBC
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl K Ar key | Fl -key Ar key | Fl -key-file Ar path
.Op Fl -iv Ar iv | Fl -iv-file Ar path
.Op Fl -text
.Op Fl S Ar n | Fl -output-size Ar n
.Ar mode
.Ar infile
.Op Ar outfile
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
encrypts or decrypts a single file using the BFCodec cipher in CBC mode.
The cipher is Blowfish-derived with custom P/S boxes.
.Pp
.Ar mode
must be
.Sy dec
(decrypt) or
.Sy enc
(encrypt).
.Ar infile
is the path to the input file; its size must be a multiple of 8 bytes.
.Ar outfile
is optional: if omitted or given as
.Sq - ,
output is written to standard output.
Writing binary data to a terminal is refused unless
.Fl -text
is set.
.Pp
Key and IV can be supplied as hex strings
.Pq Fl K Ns / Ns Fl -key ,
.Fl -iv
with spaces ignored, or as raw binary files
.Pq Fl -key-file ,
.Fl -iv-file .
A key file must be exactly 16 bytes; an IV file must be exactly 8 bytes.
The IV given as hex must be 16 hex digits (8 bytes).
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl K , Fl -key Ar key
Use
.Ar key
as the cipher key (hex string; spaces ignored).
Mutually exclusive with
.Fl -key-file .
.It Fl -key-file Ar path
Read the key from the binary file
.Ar path
(exactly 16 bytes).
Mutually exclusive with
.Fl -key .
.It Fl -iv Ar iv
Use
.Ar iv
as the initialization vector (16 hex digits = 8 bytes; spaces ignored).
Mutually exclusive with
.Fl -iv-file .
.It Fl -iv-file Ar path
Read the IV from the binary file
.Ar path
(exactly 8 bytes).
Mutually exclusive with
.Fl -iv .
.It Fl -text
Allow binary output to be written to a terminal (stdout).
.It Fl S , Fl -output-size Ar n
.Pq dec only
If the decrypted payload is larger than
.Ar n
bytes, trim the output to
.Ar n
bytes.
.Ar n
must be non-negative.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr jbt 1 ,
.Xr unjbt 1
